1
00:00:08,740 --> 00:00:13,340
Try letting go of peace, lightly.

2
00:00:20,780 --> 00:00:26,880
aiming for the setting sun
floating over the Nakagawa.

3
00:00:27,880 --> 00:00:33,980
I kicked a pebble,
and even my shoes flew off.

4
00:00:33,980 --> 00:00:42,240
So, to the carpenter
boss I had saved up for,

5
00:00:42,640 --> 00:00:48,460
they laughed that I was still just a kid.

6
00:00:49,140 --> 00:00:53,560
Even if I leave some of my energy somewhere,

7
00:00:53,560 --> 00:00:58,640
Katsushika, Kameari,
Akumi, none of it changes.

8
00:00:58,640 --> 00:01:02,540
The streetscape feels oddly gentle.

9
00:01:03,760 --> 00:01:10,500
From the pointy-hatted water intake tower,

10
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:16,780
the sunset falls toward the observatory.

11
00:01:20,480 --> 00:01:25,260
Tomorrow will end this way too, won't it.

12
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:30,280
Hey, Katsushika Shibamata,
even happiness gets lost.

13
00:01:30,280 --> 00:01:34,040
I only realized it because I'm such a fool.

14
00:01:38,920 --> 00:01:41,600
Nostradamus! The great prophecy!

15
00:01:55,300 --> 00:01:57,180
What beautiful weather today.

16
00:02:00,300 --> 00:02:03,860
Nakagawa, break something for me.

17
00:02:06,040 --> 00:02:07,800
What's wrong, senpai?

18
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:08,700
Senpai.

19
00:02:11,860 --> 00:02:15,540
I thought it was a sure bet,
so I poured my whole paycheck into it.

20
00:02:16,380 --> 00:02:20,420
Even if it threw its jockey right before the finish line,
it all vanished in an instant, poof!

21
00:02:21,420 --> 00:02:25,580
Why didn't you keep a little back
instead of betting it all on horses?

22
00:02:26,100 --> 00:02:29,960
When it's time to gamble, you go all in.
That's what a true gambler is.

23
00:02:30,380 --> 00:02:32,300
Since when did you become a gambler?

24
00:02:33,180 --> 00:02:35,640
Besides, you've been losing streak after streak lately,
haven't you?

25
00:02:36,260 --> 00:02:37,400
That's right.

26
00:02:37,400 --> 00:02:42,180
If only I had the power
to predict the future...

27
00:02:42,560 --> 00:02:44,380
I've been on a winning streak, though.

28
00:02:44,920 --> 00:02:45,880
Aaaaaah!

29
00:02:47,680 --> 00:02:48,160
Me

30
00:02:49,540 --> 00:02:50,020
Me

31
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:58,160
Super, are you alright? Super!

32
00:03:06,260 --> 00:03:08,040
My head's still spinning.

33
00:03:08,040 --> 00:03:10,600
It was a direct hit from that iron pipe,
after all.

34
00:03:11,120 --> 00:03:13,640
Even for you, Senpai,
that must've done serious damage.

35
00:03:13,640 --> 00:03:14,660
Obviously.

36
00:03:16,540 --> 00:03:19,180
Anyway, what on earth was that?

37
00:03:19,980 --> 00:03:20,600
That?

38
00:03:20,600 --> 00:03:24,000
I caught a glimpse of it
the moment the pipe hit.

39
00:03:24,440 --> 00:03:25,520
Oh no, oh no!

40
00:03:25,520 --> 00:03:26,780
The Katsushika precinct's...

41
00:03:28,160 --> 00:03:29,840
...got distracted ogling that miniskirt.

42
00:03:30,320 --> 00:03:31,760
She fell down the stairs.

43
00:03:33,160 --> 00:03:34,840
How do you know that, Ryo-chan?

44
00:03:35,180 --> 00:03:38,600
Well, I just saw that exact
same scene a moment ago.

45
00:03:38,980 --> 00:03:41,620
A moment ago,
you mean when you hit your head?

46
00:03:42,440 --> 00:03:45,700
That's it! This must be precognition!

47
00:03:45,700 --> 00:03:47,480
No way.

48
00:03:47,480 --> 00:03:50,740
Yes way! Because I bumped my head earlier,

49
00:03:50,740 --> 00:03:53,940
the unknown power hidden
inside me has awakened!

50
00:03:54,440 --> 00:03:54,820
No...

51
00:03:54,820 --> 00:03:56,960
Can something like that really happen?

52
00:03:58,160 --> 00:04:02,040
It's not impossible.
There's a famous Dutch precognitive, Peter

53
00:04:02,040 --> 00:04:07,100
Fulcos, who fell from the top of a ten-meter ladder,
and the shock of it

54
00:04:07,100 --> 00:04:12,340
awakened his hidden powers. So, Ryo-chan,
you might have psychic powers too.

55
00:04:12,820 --> 00:04:17,960
It's not just a coincidence. You can
tell if it's chance by testing it again.

56
00:04:19,320 --> 00:04:24,780
It's the Osaka specialty, a harisen chop!
Give me one good whack right here!

57
00:04:24,780 --> 00:04:28,020
No way, I can't hit my senior!

58
00:04:28,580 --> 00:04:30,480
Wouldn't a bat or something be better?

59
00:04:30,820 --> 00:04:33,440
Idiot! That would really hurt!

60
00:04:33,800 --> 00:04:36,380
Besides,
what if all the good kids at home copy us?

61
00:04:36,740 --> 00:04:39,260
Come on, Nakagawa,
give it everything you've got!

62
00:04:40,040 --> 00:04:41,460
R-really? You're sure?

63
00:04:41,940 --> 00:04:42,640
Really?

64
00:04:42,900 --> 00:04:44,600
Yes, do it, Nakagawa!

65
00:04:44,860 --> 00:04:46,160
Alright, here I go!

66
00:04:47,060 --> 00:04:48,780
Eeeh!?

67
00:04:50,600 --> 00:04:51,460
Ryo-chan!

68
00:04:51,460 --> 00:04:55,520
Whoa, I see it! I see it! Pink panties!

69
00:04:55,520 --> 00:04:57,660
Reiko, let me see for a sec.

70
00:04:57,660 --> 00:04:58,600
No way.

71
00:04:58,600 --> 00:05:00,620
Hey, this is proof of my prophecy!

72
00:05:00,620 --> 00:05:01,300
Hey, Ryo-chan!

73
00:05:01,300 --> 00:05:02,560
Come on, come on, come on.

74
00:05:05,880 --> 00:05:07,020
That's mine.

75
00:05:07,020 --> 00:05:07,920
Oh my.

76
00:05:08,760 --> 00:05:10,940
Honestly, Ryo-chan and Kei-chan,
what are you two doing?

77
00:05:10,940 --> 00:05:14,600
Sorry, it just came true so perfectly.

78
00:05:14,600 --> 00:05:18,500
But now it's proven that
I have prophetic powers!

79
00:05:18,960 --> 00:05:19,860
Is that so?

80
00:05:21,460 --> 00:05:22,860
It's just a coincidence, isn't it?

81
00:05:22,860 --> 00:05:25,600
No, I'm the reincarnation
Translation>
of that Nostradamus.

82
00:05:25,600 --> 00:05:27,020
Maybe I am.

83
00:05:27,340 --> 00:05:28,400
Nostradamus.

84
00:05:28,960 --> 00:05:31,020
That was all a fraud anyway, right?

85
00:05:31,020 --> 00:05:31,760
What?

86
00:05:32,200 --> 00:05:34,480
No, it's not entirely a lie.

87
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:36,880
Nostradamus was a 16th-century

88
00:05:36,880 --> 00:05:37,960
French prophet.

89
00:05:38,480 --> 00:05:40,580
His prophecies, written in quatrains,

90
00:05:40,900 --> 00:05:43,240
predicted the rise of Napoleon and Hitler,

91
00:05:43,640 --> 00:05:45,580
and even World War II.

92
00:05:45,580 --> 00:05:46,800
He predicted them remarkably well.

93
00:05:48,120 --> 00:05:49,980
Though the current topic is

94
00:05:51,460 --> 00:05:57,020
well, you see, I'm the reincarnation
of that Nostradamus, so to speak.

95
00:05:57,020 --> 00:06:05,160
He's just as shady-looking! The bridge prophecy is genuine!
What's all this commotion about?

96
00:06:06,960 --> 00:06:15,320
If Ryotsu is a psychic, so they say, Chief. Well, it's like the saying
"the clever hawk hides its claws," but what are you talking about?

97
00:06:15,320 --> 00:06:17,240
There's no way something
so ridiculous could happen.

98
00:06:17,240 --> 00:06:18,660
It's the truth!

99
00:06:18,660 --> 00:06:20,980
I saw the Chief fall down the stairs, and

100
00:06:20,980 --> 00:06:24,380
I clearly saw Nakagawa's underwear
color with my prophetic power.

101
00:06:24,380 --> 00:06:26,740
That's obviously just a coincidence.

102
00:06:27,540 --> 00:06:29,340
Then let's try again.

103
00:06:29,340 --> 00:06:30,280
Nakagawa.

104
00:06:30,280 --> 00:06:32,740
Yes, senpai, here I go.

105
00:06:36,600 --> 00:06:37,580
I see it.

106
00:06:37,580 --> 00:06:40,940
The Chief's dinner tonight
is an assortment of sashimi.

107
00:06:40,940 --> 00:06:42,460
I see. And then?

108
00:06:42,460 --> 00:06:43,780
And then...

109
00:06:43,780 --> 00:06:44,640
Here goes.

110
00:06:49,960 --> 00:06:52,700
Tomorrow's breakfast
is dried horse mackerel.

111
00:06:53,120 --> 00:06:55,980
Well, if all you can predict is things like that,
there's no helping it.

112
00:06:55,980 --> 00:06:58,240
Kei-chan, this time I'll do it.

113
00:06:58,240 --> 00:06:58,800
Yes.

114
00:06:59,520 --> 00:07:01,240
Here I come, Ryo-chan.

115
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:04,840
Wait, Reiko,
you don't need to strain so hard.

116
00:07:04,840 --> 00:07:06,020
No arguments!

117
00:07:07,020 --> 00:07:07,560
Whoa!

118
00:07:09,578 --> 00:07:14,840
Ryo-chan, are you okay?

119
00:07:15,640 --> 00:07:16,680
I'm not okay.

120
00:07:17,460 --> 00:07:18,880
More importantly, this is serious!

121
00:07:18,980 --> 00:07:23,480
The wanted phantom thief No.
707 is hitting Potato Bank tonight!

122
00:07:23,660 --> 00:07:25,800
What?! Is that true, Ryotsu?!

123
00:07:38,880 --> 00:07:42,580
Thief 707, you're under arrest
for breaking into a safe in the act.

124
00:07:42,580 --> 00:07:43,020
What?

125
00:07:43,700 --> 00:07:46,620
I know everything you were planning to do.

126
00:07:54,240 --> 00:07:56,580
Well done, Ryotsu, that's a great catch!

127
00:07:56,580 --> 00:07:58,020
Ryo-chan, that's amazing!

128
00:07:58,020 --> 00:07:59,960
Even Nostradamus would be impressed.

129
00:07:59,960 --> 00:08:06,880
Hey, from today on, call me Starnyon,
the official Great Prophet.

130
00:08:06,880 --> 00:08:08,880
Eeeeeeeh!

131
00:08:14,120 --> 00:08:16,000
Ross, go along with both of them.

132
00:08:17,100 --> 00:08:17,480
me

133
00:08:23,420 --> 00:08:25,480
What a huge number of reporters.

134
00:08:25,480 --> 00:08:29,300
Well, everyone has at least
one thing going for them

135
00:08:32,740 --> 00:08:36,780
With this prophetic power,
I'll win every horse and bicycle race.

136
00:08:36,780 --> 00:08:39,120
That means I'll be a millionaire in no time.

137
00:08:39,120 --> 00:08:40,600
Here goes!

138
00:08:40,600 --> 00:08:45,540
Tomorrow's weather: cloudy, then rain.

139
00:08:47,480 --> 00:08:52,740
Percent...
no, wrong, this isn't it. Here goes!

140
00:08:53,680 --> 00:09:00,140
Yeah! "The Chief will scold me again today, right?"
Whoa, no, that's wrong!

141
00:09:00,800 --> 00:09:06,820
Why can't they build a site for horse and bicycle racing?
This is such a waste of treasure.

142
00:09:07,960 --> 00:09:10,200
Here it comes! Starnyon!

143
00:09:12,480 --> 00:09:13,900
Today, I'll make just one prophecy.

144
00:09:13,900 --> 00:09:15,820
Let's make it something
with a nice ring to it.

145
00:09:16,380 --> 00:09:17,780
Wh-wait, hold on!

146
00:09:17,780 --> 00:09:20,200
You can't make prophecies so lightly.

147
00:09:21,360 --> 00:09:22,100
Wait a moment.

148
00:09:22,100 --> 00:09:25,100
Even if horse and bicycle racing fail,
this method still works!

149
00:09:25,720 --> 00:09:27,240
A great prophet, you say?

150
00:09:27,420 --> 00:09:28,920
What are you getting at, Ryotsu?

151
00:09:28,920 --> 00:09:30,000
Well, you see,

152
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:33,800
at this turn of the century,
every resident is harboring some anxiety.

153
00:09:33,800 --> 00:09:35,440
So, these anxieties -

154
00:09:35,440 --> 00:09:38,620
I intend to relieve them
with my prophetic powers.

155
00:09:39,500 --> 00:09:42,320
You're not plotting something shady again,
are you?

156
00:09:42,320 --> 00:09:43,840
H-how can you say that, I'm joking!

157
00:09:43,840 --> 00:09:46,300
It's purely a public
service for the residents!

158
00:09:47,840 --> 00:09:51,100
But I've never heard of a great prophet

159
00:09:52,340 --> 00:09:53,860
I have a bad feeling about this.

160
00:09:53,860 --> 00:09:55,480
I've got a bad feeling.

161
00:09:55,480 --> 00:09:56,480
W-what?

162
00:09:56,480 --> 00:10:00,040
Mr. President, you fell down the
stairs and got hurt before, didn't you?

163
00:10:01,520 --> 00:10:04,460
This time, something even worse is -

164
00:10:05,120 --> 00:10:06,180
W-what did you say?

165
00:10:06,180 --> 00:10:08,300
What on earth is going to happen?

166
00:10:08,620 --> 00:10:12,380
I'll ease those anxious feelings
with my great prophecies.

167
00:10:12,380 --> 00:10:16,480
A great prophet is what
humanity needs for world peace.

168
00:10:16,480 --> 00:10:17,660
Understand?

169
00:10:28,300 --> 00:10:32,440
I should at least charge
10,000 yen per reading.

170
00:10:32,440 --> 00:10:35,220
10,000 yen per reading, you say?

171
00:11:04,820 --> 00:11:06,680
I can tell just by looking at this face.

172
00:11:07,380 --> 00:11:08,180
Y-yes?

173
00:11:08,880 --> 00:11:09,540
Actually,

174
00:11:09,540 --> 00:11:10,480
wait a moment.

175
00:11:11,080 --> 00:11:13,860
I think steak fortune-telling suits you.

176
00:11:13,860 --> 00:11:15,640
Steak fortune-telling?

177
00:11:15,780 --> 00:11:16,340
Come on, now.

178
00:11:16,340 --> 00:11:19,660
Everyone has a fortune-telling
method that suits them best.

179
00:11:19,660 --> 00:11:22,080
Bring me a steak right away.

180
00:11:22,080 --> 00:11:24,680
Cook it medium-rare.

181
00:11:27,560 --> 00:11:29,320
M-making for a pretty good meat, this.

182
00:11:29,320 --> 00:11:31,120
You've got the right attitude, you know.

183
00:11:31,120 --> 00:11:32,160
Th-thanks, I guess.

184
00:11:32,860 --> 00:11:34,420
So, what is it you want
me to divine for you?

185
00:11:34,820 --> 00:11:38,020
You don't need to say it.
I already know everything.

186
00:11:39,620 --> 00:11:40,980
I see... ahead of you.

187
00:11:41,480 --> 00:11:44,120
Go down the path you've been thinking of.

188
00:11:44,220 --> 00:11:46,660
Then the way will open up before you.

189
00:11:46,920 --> 00:11:47,700
Really? Ryotsu?

190
00:11:48,360 --> 00:11:50,500
You'll address me as Nostra-Ryotsu-sama.

191
00:11:50,600 --> 00:11:52,980
What I say is never wrong.

192
00:11:53,420 --> 00:11:55,480
Alright, I was hesitating,
but I've made up my mind.

193
00:11:55,800 --> 00:11:58,220
I'm going to get another
limited-edition figure.

194
00:11:58,760 --> 00:11:59,780
Just you wait, Saori.

195
00:12:02,220 --> 00:12:03,920
Idiots are easy to manipulate.

196
00:12:04,820 --> 00:12:05,420
Next person?

197
00:12:06,300 --> 00:12:06,980
Excuse me...

198
00:12:07,400 --> 00:12:10,300
Your face shows the signs
of coffee fortune-telling.

199
00:12:10,300 --> 00:12:12,600
Bring me a coffee right away.

200
00:12:16,320 --> 00:12:19,020
Mm, after-meal coffee is good, isn't it?

201
00:12:19,440 --> 00:12:20,840
About the fortune-telling...

202
00:12:20,840 --> 00:12:22,420
I know, I know.

203
00:12:22,420 --> 00:12:24,320
I'm about to tell your fortune now.

204
00:12:27,060 --> 00:12:28,700
Th-this is...

205
00:12:29,020 --> 00:12:30,860
Th-the romance with my girlfriend?

206
00:12:31,500 --> 00:12:33,980
As long as she's in love with you,
it'll go well.

207
00:12:34,820 --> 00:12:36,400
If she dislikes you, it's hopeless.

208
00:12:36,400 --> 00:12:37,520
Got it?

209
00:12:37,520 --> 00:12:39,100
More or less.

210
00:12:39,100 --> 00:12:40,220
Good.

211
00:12:40,220 --> 00:12:42,020
Alright, next person!

212
00:12:42,560 --> 00:12:43,080
Please, go ahead.

213
00:12:44,480 --> 00:12:47,820
For you, I'd say massage
fortune-telling is the best choice.

214
00:12:47,820 --> 00:12:49,720
Massage fortune-telling?

215
00:12:53,560 --> 00:12:55,180
Can you tell how it's going?

216
00:12:55,180 --> 00:12:57,480
Hey, don't stop moving your hands.

217
00:12:57,480 --> 00:13:00,860
Your futures are just
starting to become clear to me.

218
00:13:00,860 --> 00:13:01,660
Really.

219
00:13:01,660 --> 00:13:03,300
Well, it can't be helped.

220
00:13:04,820 --> 00:13:06,620
A bit harder there.

221
00:13:07,400 --> 00:13:10,280
Your futures are gradually coming into view.

222
00:13:11,780 --> 00:13:14,820
Ryotsu, I'd like you to read my fortune too.

223
00:13:15,340 --> 00:13:17,580
Very well, then take off your jacket.

224
00:13:22,060 --> 00:13:23,580
What are you doing, Ryotsu?

225
00:13:23,580 --> 00:13:27,880
It's rope-mark fortune-telling, Chief.
I read the marks the rope leaves behind.

226
00:13:28,520 --> 00:13:29,620
W-what?

227
00:13:29,620 --> 00:13:31,940
The rope marks are faint.

228
00:13:31,940 --> 00:13:34,580
Well, that's enough for now, right?

229
00:13:34,580 --> 00:13:35,940
Aaaaaah!

230
00:13:39,860 --> 00:13:48,780
Things are taking a strange turn, aren't they?
That's Ryo-chan's usual bad habit. Ryotsu-kun, read my fortune... understood.

231
00:13:49,380 --> 00:13:52,780
Then how about candle-wax
torture fortune-telling?

232
00:13:59,580 --> 00:14:00,840
Flight fortune-telling?

233
00:14:01,040 --> 00:14:01,560
Be sharp, you two.

234
00:14:01,560 --> 00:14:04,380
Now, take out your bills.

235
00:14:04,380 --> 00:14:05,320
R-right.

236
00:14:06,120 --> 00:14:07,880
With these, we make paper airplanes.

237
00:14:07,880 --> 00:14:09,700
While thinking of your wish, of course.

238
00:14:09,700 --> 00:14:13,780
Then we fly this airplane all
the way to that stand over there.

239
00:14:14,420 --> 00:14:14,820
There you go!

240
00:14:17,920 --> 00:14:20,820
If it lands neatly, your wish comes true.

241
00:14:20,820 --> 00:14:27,820
The higher the bill, the more blessings you get: a thousand yen,
five thousand, ten thousand!

242
00:14:27,820 --> 00:14:29,780
Come on, everyone, let's give it a try!

243
00:14:29,780 --> 00:14:30,440
Alright!

244
00:14:31,060 --> 00:14:32,020
One, two, three!

245
00:14:33,460 --> 00:14:39,000
What a shame.
Your wishes didn't come true, did they?

246
00:14:39,840 --> 00:14:41,420
That money...

247
00:14:41,420 --> 00:14:44,660
This isn't money, it's a wish airplane!

248
00:14:44,660 --> 00:14:48,000
If they don't come true, we'll hold a
memorial service for the wishes here, you know.

249
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:49,100
B-but...

250
00:14:50,820 --> 00:14:51,940
You'll surely win, I promise!

251
00:14:51,940 --> 00:14:52,540
Yes.

252
00:14:53,020 --> 00:14:53,920
Hey!

253
00:14:54,200 --> 00:14:54,920
Ryotsu!

254
00:14:55,780 --> 00:14:58,480
Didn't I tell you a hundred
times not to take money?!

255
00:14:59,480 --> 00:15:01,040
I'm not taking money!

256
00:15:01,160 --> 00:15:03,300
This is called a wish airplane,

257
00:15:03,300 --> 00:15:05,860
Shut up! Give it back right now!

258
00:15:09,280 --> 00:15:11,300
A sign of misfortune is showing!

259
00:15:11,540 --> 00:15:12,060
What?

260
00:15:12,540 --> 00:15:14,780
Let's do a detailed reading
with shogi fortune-telling.

261
00:15:15,420 --> 00:15:18,400
Annyepapara pa, fundorabejū!

262
00:15:19,900 --> 00:15:21,320
Ow

263
00:15:21,320 --> 00:15:22,180
T-this is...

264
00:15:22,180 --> 00:15:23,320
W-what is it?

265
00:15:24,040 --> 00:15:25,480
Good grief, a hundred warriors!

266
00:15:26,420 --> 00:15:28,040
Now, let's perform an exorcism.

267
00:15:31,020 --> 00:15:40,280
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

268
00:15:40,280 --> 00:15:41,700
That kind of thing doesn't exist!

269
00:15:41,860 --> 00:15:43,640
You're possessed, you know!

270
00:15:43,720 --> 00:15:44,920
Wake up!

271
00:15:45,300 --> 00:15:45,940
Bujaaa!

272
00:15:46,100 --> 00:15:46,620
Hah!

273
00:15:47,540 --> 00:15:48,760
You evil spirit!

274
00:15:48,840 --> 00:15:50,980
Try taking the form of the Chief!

275
00:15:51,400 --> 00:15:53,580
I told you, you've got it wrong!

276
00:15:54,420 --> 00:15:55,760
Oharai-gii!

277
00:15:59,580 --> 00:16:01,520
The evil spirit has been driven off.

278
00:16:01,520 --> 00:16:02,980
That's great!

279
00:16:03,840 --> 00:16:05,280
There's no such thing!

280
00:16:05,500 --> 00:16:07,900
How dare you possess me, you evil spirit!

281
00:16:08,020 --> 00:16:09,140
Color! Color! Color!

282
00:16:10,300 --> 00:16:11,780
This is getting weirder and weirder.

283
00:16:12,220 --> 00:16:14,720
Maybe Ryotsu's losing his psychic powers.

284
00:16:18,220 --> 00:16:20,980
His fortunes never come true.

285
00:16:21,440 --> 00:16:25,280
He says the lucky color is camel,
and nothing good has happened at all.

286
00:16:25,280 --> 00:16:27,420
Mine was "death blow" color.

287
00:16:27,880 --> 00:16:31,280
The limited edition Dokimemo
figure I blew my whole paycheck on.

288
00:16:31,700 --> 00:16:35,240
It was a fake,
and I got ripped off by Ryotsu for it.

289
00:16:35,240 --> 00:16:38,060
He told me I'd get along with my girlfriend,
and then I got dumped.

290
00:16:38,060 --> 00:16:39,020
My wings fell off.

291
00:16:39,020 --> 00:16:39,920
I fell into a ditch.

292
00:16:39,920 --> 00:16:41,080
My car got smashed up.

293
00:16:42,200 --> 00:16:44,780
Let's go file a complaint! What's with this
"Nostradamus" nonsense!

294
00:16:49,040 --> 00:16:50,500
We made quite a bit of money, didn't we?

295
00:16:50,500 --> 00:16:51,120
Senpai

296
00:16:51,120 --> 00:16:54,060
What's wrong, Nakagawa?

297
00:16:54,060 --> 00:16:54,840
Well, it's just that...

298
00:16:55,800 --> 00:16:57,740
they're saying Ryo-chan's
fortune-telling is a scam.

299
00:16:57,740 --> 00:17:01,020
Komachi-chan and the others have formed
a victims' alliance with everyone.

300
00:17:01,020 --> 00:17:02,620
They're heading this way.

301
00:17:03,100 --> 00:17:03,720
What?!

302
00:17:03,720 --> 00:17:05,400
Ryotsu Kankichi is here!

303
00:17:05,400 --> 00:17:05,860
Right?

304
00:17:08,400 --> 00:17:10,940
Well, well, look who's all here.

305
00:17:10,940 --> 00:17:12,700
What business do you have with me?

306
00:17:13,500 --> 00:17:15,220
"What business"? Don't play dumb!

307
00:17:15,780 --> 00:17:16,640
You've caused trouble for everyone!

308
00:17:16,920 --> 00:17:19,360
Not one of your predictions came true!

309
00:17:19,600 --> 00:17:20,380
Some luck you've got

310
00:17:21,100 --> 00:17:22,380
Hmph, what are you talking about!

311
00:17:22,540 --> 00:17:26,000
My powers of foresight
haven't declined one bit!

312
00:17:26,280 --> 00:17:28,700
I bet the first one was
just a lucky guess, right?

313
00:17:28,800 --> 00:17:30,000
You fraud!

314
00:17:30,480 --> 00:17:32,500
Hmph, you bunch of fools...

315
00:17:32,500 --> 00:17:35,960
I'll show you the greatness
of my powers of foresight!

316
00:17:36,100 --> 00:17:36,780
Nakagawa!

317
00:17:37,260 --> 00:17:38,680
Yes! Here goes!

318
00:17:42,900 --> 00:17:45,980
What are you waiting for?
Hurry up and make your prediction!

319
00:17:47,240 --> 00:17:49,080
Nakagawa, harder!

320
00:17:49,080 --> 00:17:50,500
Yes, senpai!

321
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:58,160
Oh no, my powers of prediction
vanished right when I needed them!

322
00:17:58,940 --> 00:18:01,180
So it was just a lucky guess after all.

323
00:18:01,180 --> 00:18:01,900
N-no, it's not!

324
00:18:01,900 --> 00:18:04,460
Then go on, make a prediction.

325
00:18:04,920 --> 00:18:08,060
A prophecy, a prophecy, a prophecy!

326
00:18:08,880 --> 00:18:10,840
Well, say something already!

327
00:18:10,840 --> 00:18:13,860
T-to... T-to... Tokyo Bay...

328
00:18:13,860 --> 00:18:15,480
Into Tokyo Bay...

329
00:18:15,480 --> 00:18:18,320
When the tide comes in...

330
00:18:18,320 --> 00:18:19,580
And then...

331
00:18:20,840 --> 00:18:23,080
The Sumida River will overflow...

332
00:18:23,080 --> 00:18:27,840
An ancient demon will revive
and show its form once again!

333
00:18:27,840 --> 00:18:29,580
An ancient demon?

334
00:18:29,820 --> 00:18:31,980
Y-yes, a demon.

335
00:18:31,980 --> 00:18:32,600
When?

336
00:18:32,600 --> 00:18:36,240
Um... this coming Sunday, I think.

337
00:18:36,240 --> 00:18:38,360
That's obviously a lie.

338
00:18:38,680 --> 00:18:39,380
It's not a lie!

339
00:18:39,800 --> 00:18:43,343
Those who don't believe my fortune-telling
will incur the demon's wrath,

340
00:18:43,393 --> 00:18:45,680
and vanish like flotsam on the open sea!

341
00:18:46,160 --> 00:18:48,540
I said I don't believe it, and I meant it!

342
00:18:49,160 --> 00:18:50,140
Fine, then.

343
00:18:50,190 --> 00:18:54,020
If it doesn't come true, all of you
will have to pay my doctor's fees.

344
00:18:54,760 --> 00:18:56,120
Fine by me.

345
00:18:56,580 --> 00:18:59,780
Don't come crying to me later. Let's go.

346
00:19:00,120 --> 00:19:00,820
What?

347
00:19:02,780 --> 00:19:05,740
Senpai, is this really okay?
Making a promise like that.

348
00:19:05,940 --> 00:19:08,360
Did you just make that up on the spot?

349
00:19:10,200 --> 00:19:13,740
Don't worry.
Nostradamus's prophecies always come true.

350
00:19:14,700 --> 00:19:18,520
Según... by Mr. Nostradamus,
said to be the last prophet of this century,

351
00:19:18,520 --> 00:19:21,800
here on the Sumida River, where the
appearance of a demon has been prophesied,

352
00:19:21,800 --> 00:19:26,120
crowds of people have gathered,
eager to see the truth with their own eyes.

353
00:19:27,380 --> 00:19:32,260
Food stalls have appeared in nearby Sumida Park,
along with shops selling prophecy goods,

354
00:19:32,260 --> 00:19:34,720
and the area is buzzing with
an unexpected demon fever.

355
00:19:34,720 --> 00:19:37,600
Okay, okay,
admission is 1,000 yen per person.

356
00:19:38,680 --> 00:19:45,240
Bringing a camera costs 10,000 yen,
and 30% of the stall sales are mine.

357
00:19:45,240 --> 00:19:51,140
What a windfall! I'd better collect
viewing fees from the sightseeing boats too.

358
00:19:52,660 --> 00:20:03,320
Yes, 1,000 yen per person. Senpai, you seem so relaxed, but will it really be alright?
That prophecy from earlier sounded so fishy.

359
00:20:03,680 --> 00:20:06,520
If all this commotion
happens and nothing appears,

360
00:20:06,520 --> 00:20:08,020
you'll be in big trouble.

361
00:20:17,440 --> 00:20:20,800
Now the predicted high tide is finally here.

362
00:20:21,460 --> 00:20:24,200
Will the great prophecy really come true?

363
00:20:24,200 --> 00:20:26,880
What exactly is this thing?

364
00:20:27,720 --> 00:20:30,360
Is it heralding the destruction of mankind?

365
00:20:30,360 --> 00:20:32,720
That moment is about to arrive.

366
00:20:33,860 --> 00:20:34,560
It's here!

367
00:20:38,080 --> 00:20:40,228
I-it's coming!

368
00:20:40,278 --> 00:20:44,400
Is this the ancient demon?

369
00:20:45,080 --> 00:20:49,060
What is its true identity?
And what will become of mankind's fate?

370
00:20:55,260 --> 00:20:56,620
W-what is this!

371
00:20:59,980 --> 00:21:01,560
It's a dinosaur!

372
00:21:01,860 --> 00:21:05,120
The ancient demon was a dinosaur
brought back to life in modern times!

373
00:21:05,560 --> 00:21:05,900
Whoa!

374
00:21:06,860 --> 00:21:09,160
Behold, the prophecy has come true!

375
00:21:10,020 --> 00:21:10,820
N-no way!

376
00:21:11,560 --> 00:21:12,360
Look at that lie!

377
00:21:12,820 --> 00:21:15,320
That something like this
would actually happen!

378
00:21:15,640 --> 00:21:19,080
Demon, calm your rage and return to the sea!

379
00:21:23,900 --> 00:21:27,340
Mr. Ryotsu is trying to calm the
demon with his spiritual power.

380
00:21:34,120 --> 00:21:35,940
It's going back into the water!

381
00:21:44,320 --> 00:21:45,260
Papier-mâché.

382
00:21:46,020 --> 00:21:47,400
Sorry, Ryotsu.

383
00:21:47,800 --> 00:21:50,140
No matter how well I
know weapons in general,

384
00:21:50,140 --> 00:21:52,480
I can't pilot a submarine.

385
00:21:53,600 --> 00:21:58,940
Hey, what did you think I borrowed that
submarine from Yokosuka without permission for?

386
00:21:59,560 --> 00:22:01,980
What, so it was a fraud after all,
wasn't it?

387
00:22:29,220 --> 00:22:31,440
You took a submarine from the
US military without permission,

388
00:22:31,490 --> 00:22:33,360
and you think you'll get off scot-free?

389
00:22:44,420 --> 00:22:46,200
What are you doing? Dive, quick!

390
00:22:46,400 --> 00:22:47,440
Easy for you to say!

391
00:22:48,300 --> 00:22:49,460
Ahhhh!

392
00:22:50,280 --> 00:22:53,260
Oh no! I pressed some kind of switch!

393
00:22:53,480 --> 00:22:56,120
Whoa! That's the anti-aircraft giant switch!

394
00:23:06,320 --> 00:23:08,400
Why is it coming this way?

395
00:23:24,820 --> 00:23:26,520
We somehow survived.

396
00:23:28,240 --> 00:23:29,280
Hey, Ryo!

397
00:23:29,280 --> 00:23:30,040
Chief.

398
00:23:30,040 --> 00:23:33,900
What have you done, you big idiot!

399
00:23:33,900 --> 00:23:36,540
But Chief, my prophecy came true!

400
00:23:36,540 --> 00:23:39,540
Didn't everyone vanish
into the sea like driftwood?

401
00:23:39,980 --> 00:23:43,740
You idiot, I'll leave you sunk down
there for the rest of your life.

402
00:23:43,740 --> 00:23:46,480
Wait.

403
00:23:48,440 --> 00:23:53,200
Ryotsu, you may be the terror king Nostradamus prophesied,
you know.

404
00:23:54,100 --> 00:23:54,900
Worst.

405
00:23:56,900 --> 00:23:59,480
I hate Nostradamus.

406
00:24:58,520 --> 00:25:02,140
I surely want to confess,

407
00:25:02,800 --> 00:25:07,900
but somehow, only love is out of tune,

408
00:25:07,900 --> 00:25:15,800
don't hide everything behind your bravado.

409
00:25:31,380 --> 00:25:37,500
Next time preview.

